    "summary": "Roth IRAs and Traditional IRAs both offer tax advantages for retirement savings but differ in when taxes are applied — Traditional IRAs provide an upfront deduction with taxable withdrawals, while Roth IRAs use after-tax contributions for tax-free retirement income. The best choice depends on your…",
