    "summary": "SPF measures how much UVB radiation a sunscreen blocks, but the scale is non-linear — SPF 30 blocks ~97% and SPF 50 blocks ~98%, making the jump far less dramatic than the numbers suggest. Most dermatologists recommend a minimum of SPF 30, with SPF 50 for extended or high-risk sun exposure, and…",
